# 3.1 Testing Quality Objectives
- Verify Jira API authentication and access permissions.
- Ensure issue description is available for downstream processing.

# 3.2 Test Scope
## 3.2.1 In Scope
- Jira API authentication validation
- Error handling for missing/unauthorized issue access

## 3.2.2 Out of Scope
- Requirement analysis for AD-488 (content unavailable)
- Testing of business features described in AD-488

# 4. Test Strategy
## 4.1 Test Approach
Testing will focus on:
- API/service integration layer to validate authentication outcomes during issue retrieval.
- Workflow-control behavior to ensure downstream processing is blocked when the issue description is unavailable.
- Negative-path coverage for 401 Unauthorized handling, error propagation, and traceable logs for failed access attempts.
- Decision-based scenarios to verify only valid authentication and available description permit progression.
- No business-feature or requirement-content testing (explicitly out of scope).

